fix: Verified review findings, fixed projection order, reverted the global heat vision forcing

Review findings, verified against the code before acting:

  P2 xrGame/Level_start.cpp:211/213 - real. string64 CDKey (64 bytes) written by
     sscanf(start, "%[^/]") with no width, input from the command line: any key longer than 63
     characters overflows the stack. Fixed with sscanf_s and %63. The sibling four lines above
     had the same defect (else xr_strcpy(PasswordStr, PSW) unbounded) and was fixed too.
  P3 xrGame/Actor.cpp:1474/1490 - real but latent. char buffer[128] / char rank_name[100] filled
     with sprintf from a Lua returned faction/rank name: unbounded. Both now snprintf with sizeof.
  P3 r4_R_render imaging restore - real. The value captured when the lens engaged was restored on
     release, so a console change made while aiming was overwritten and lost. The block now
     remembers what it last wrote and adopts any other value as the new one to restore.
  P4 device.h SvpScopeState - theoretical, not reachable. Checked every reader: the game side
     reads exactly one field (lens_rendered in Actor.cpp), everything else is render side only,
     so no half written combination can be observed. Documented with the rule to keep it that way.
  TargetSVP residency - real, and the comment hid half of it. The set is created on first aim,
     never evicted while idle (only on an extent change or shutdown); that is deliberate, since
     evicting would reallocate the scene chain and hitch on the next aim. Comment corrected.

Projection order: the publish diagnostic measured sampled spans of 0.6 and 1.5 where the applied
magnification asks for 0.33, and the rectangular, unmagnified, dark lens follows from sampling
past the texture border. In row vector algebra a main view NDC maps by p * inv(vp_main) * vp_lens,
so the product must be inv(vp_main) * vp_lens; the previous order was the temporal upscaler's and
answers a different question. Transposing on upload stays, since the pack's shader uses mul(M, v).

Heat vision forcing reverted: the same session showed that driving ps_r2_heatvision from the optic
turned the whole screen into a black heat vision frame (the console variable bypasses the upscaler,
disables the flare path, selects a heat vision shader element and expects the heat mask the device
path fills). The optic's imaging identity is still read and logged - and the read works, the log
shows img=3 thermal=1 for wpn_rsass_echo1, resolved from [echo1] through the token suffix walk -
but rendering the heat look into the lens target only is left as the remaining piece rather than
flipping a frame level switch.